---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ConfirmOfficial from "../components/ConfirmOfficial.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Passive residency in 2026"
  description="Andorra passive residency 2026: €1m investment, €50k AFA payment, 90 days, quota. What the law now costs."
  path="/passive-residency"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Passive residency in 2026</h1>
    <p>
      You may live here without working. You may not treat this as a
      cheap golden visa. The 2026 law raised both the capital and the
      character of the state payment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <p class="as-of">As of 29 August 2026</p>
    <ConfirmOfficial />

    <p>
      As of 29 August 2026, a new authorisation of residence without
      lucrative activity generally requires a permanent, effective
      investment of €1,000,000 in qualifying Andorran assets, an AFA
      contribution of €50,000 for the main applicant and €12,000 per
      dependent, private health and pension cover, a place to live, a
      clean record, and 90 days in Andorra each calendar year. You
      cannot take Andorran employment. Quota can close.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal baseline: Llei 2/2026, of 22 January, in force 13 February
      2026, amending the immigration and investment rules built in Llei
      5/2025. Always re-read the current text on
      <a
        href="https://bopadocuments.blob.core.windows.net/bopa-documents/038015/pdf/CGL_2026_02_12_10_11_12.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">BOPA — Llei 2/2026</a
      >
      and the Immigration pages on
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia/residencia-sense-treball-autoritzacio-inicial"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Govern.ad</a
      >
      before you transfer money.
    </p>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>
      People who can live on assets or foreign income, will not work in
      Andorra, can actually spend 90 days here, and can show the million
      and the AFA payment without inventing a story about where the
      money came from.
    </p>

    <h2>Who should not use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Anyone who will work here. That is the active route. See
        <a href="/company-active-residency">Company and active residency</a>.
      </li>
      <li>Anyone who cannot do 90 days in the calendar year.</li>
      <li>
        Anyone still quoting 2019–2024 thresholds as if they were the
        current law.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The numbers</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Item</th>
          <th>Working figure</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Investment</td>
          <td>
            €1,000,000 in qualifying Andorran assets, permanent and
            effective.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>If using property</td>
          <td>
            €800,000 minimum per dwelling or unit. The million is the
            investment total; the unit floor is separate.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Housing Fund route</td>
          <td>
            Often cited at €400,000 if placed permanently in the Fons
            d’Habitatge. Confirm the fund exists and is open before you
            plan around it. Think of that figure as a legal possibility,
            not a counter you can walk up to.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>AFA contribution</td>
          <td>€50,000 main applicant + €12,000 per dependent.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Refund?</td>
          <td>
            Working rule for files granted under Llei 2/2026: the sum is
            a fons perdut — kept if the permit is granted, returned if
            the initial application is refused. Some secondary pages
            describe a 30k/20k split. Treat that as a conflict. Confirm
            with AFA and your gestoria before you pay.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Days</td>
          <td>90 per calendar year, not necessarily consecutive.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Work in Andorra</td>
          <td>No.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cover</td>
          <td>
            Private health, and the pension / incapacity cover
            Immigration asks for at the time.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Quota</td>
          <td>
            Authorisations without work can be capped. Ask whether the
            current year still has slots before you start the file.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Timeline</td>
          <td>
            Often quoted at two to four months for a complete file.
            Incomplete files take longer. Nobody can honestly promise a
            date.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Professional fees</td>
          <td>
            Budget €3,000–€8,000 for a straightforward file, more if the
            source-of-wealth story is complicated.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Card tariffs</td>
          <td>
            Govern.ad currently lists €3,000 for delivery of a
            residence-without-work authorisation, €1,000 for a dependant,
            and €500 for renewal. Confirm the
            <a
              href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/altres-tramits/tarifes"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">tariffs page</a
            >.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What the million can sit in</h2>
    <p>
      Article 96 of Llei 2/2026 names Andorran assets: property; equity
      in resident companies; certain debt or collective-investment
      instruments of resident issuers, for a maximum of 36 months before
      the sum must move to another permitted class; public-administration
      debt; life-insurance products with resident insurers; or
      unremunerated AFA deposits. If the investment is made wholly or
      partly in property, the same article requires more than €800,000
      on each immovable unit. The million-euro total still applies.
    </p>

    <h2>The file in order</h2>
    <p>
      Passport, apostilled police certificates, proof of a place to
      live, evidence of means and of the investment, private health and
      pension cover, the medical exam Immigration names, civil-status
      papers if anyone is joining you, and the AFA payment. The bank
      will want the source-of-wealth story before the AFA money moves.
      Build that pack as one file. See
      <a href="/the-file">The file and the bank</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What usually breaks it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Source of wealth that does not survive a bank or AFA question.
      </li>
      <li>Police certificates without the apostille, or from the wrong years.</li>
      <li>
        Treating a Barcelona commute as 90 days in Andorra. The days
        have to be here.
      </li>
      <li>
        Paying the AFA sum as if it were still a refundable bond. For
        new files under Llei 2/2026 it is generally a payment.
      </li>
      <li>
        A unit under €800,000 offered as the whole property leg of the
        investment.
      </li>
      <li>Starting a file after the quota for the year has closed.</li>
      <li>
        Planning around a Housing Fund blog post without checking that
        the Fons d’Habitatge is open and will take the money.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Related:
      <a href="/residency-vs-tax">Three things people confuse</a>,
      <a href="/buying-property">Buying property</a>,
      <a href="/the-file">The file and the bank</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
